(function(E){ const x = E["exam-03"] = E["exam-03"] || {units:{}}; (x.units = x.units || {})["x03-l3"] = {"id":"x03-l3","patterns":["L3-science","PARA-opinion"],"title":{"en":"Listening Part 3: planning a project","tr":"Listening Part 3: bir proje planlamak","fa":"Listening Part 3: برنامه‌ریزی یک پروژه"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to follow two students planning research: choose the reasons and methods they agree on, ignore the ideas they drop, and match six items to the opinions in a box of eight.","tr":"Bu derste bir araştırma planlayan iki öğrenciyi takip etmeyi öğreneceksin: üzerinde anlaştıkları nedenleri ve yöntemleri seçecek, bıraktıkları fikirleri dikkate almayacak ve altı öğeyi sekiz seçenekli bir kutudaki görüşlerle eşleştireceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری صحبت دو دانشجو را که پژوهشی را برنامه‌ریزی می‌کنند دنبال کنی: دلیل‌ها و روش‌هایی را که روی آن‌ها توافق دارند انتخاب کنی، ایده‌هایی را که کنار می‌گذارند نادیده بگیری و شش مورد را به نظرهای یک کادر هشت‌تایی وصل کنی."},"sessions":[["explain"],["drill"],["exit"]],"explain":{"title":{"en":"Listening Part 3: planning a project","tr":"Listening Part 3: bir proje planlamak","fa":"Listening Part 3: برنامه‌ریزی یک پروژه"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to follow two students planning research: choose the reasons and methods they agree on, ignore the ideas they drop, and match six items to the opinions in a box of eight.","tr":"Bu derste bir araştırma planlayan iki öğrenciyi takip etmeyi öğreneceksin: üzerinde anlaştıkları nedenleri ve yöntemleri seçecek, bıraktıkları fikirleri dikkate almayacak ve altı öğeyi sekiz seçenekli bir kutudaki görüşlerle eşleştireceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری صحبت دو دانشجو را که پژوهشی را برنامه‌ریزی می‌کنند دنبال کنی: دلیل‌ها و روش‌هایی را که روی آن‌ها توافق دارند انتخاب کنی، ایده‌هایی را که کنار می‌گذارند نادیده بگیری و شش مورد را به نظرهای یک کادر هشت‌تایی وصل کنی."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"10"},{"label":{"en":"Speakers","tr":"Konuşan","fa":"گوینده"},"value":"2"},{"label":{"en":"Box","tr":"Kutu","fa":"کادر"},"value":"A-H"}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ بافت"},"head":{"en":"This exam: repairing and reusing clothes","tr":"Bu sınav: giysileri onarmak ve yeniden kullanmak","fa":"این آزمون: تعمیر و استفاده‌ی دوباره از لباس"},"intro":{"en":"Part 3 is students discussing their studies. Planning a project (choosing a topic, choosing methods, predicting results) is one of the commonest situations, and the questions test what the two speakers finally agree on.","tr":"Part 3, öğrencilerin dersleri hakkındaki konuşmasıdır. Bir proje planlamak (konu ve yöntem seçmek, sonuçları tahmin etmek) en yaygın durumlardandır ve sorular iki konuşanın sonunda neyde anlaştığını ölçer.","fa":"Part 3 گفتگوی دانشجوها درباره‌ی درسشان است. برنامه‌ریزی یک پروژه (انتخاب موضوع، انتخاب روش، پیش‌بینی نتیجه) از رایج‌ترین موقعیت‌هاست و سؤال‌ها می‌سنجند دو گوینده در نهایت روی چه چیزی توافق می‌کنند."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب را می‌آورند"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x03-l3-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["L3-science","PARA-opinion"],"often":{"pattern":"L3-science","n":19,"of":40,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 19 of the last 40 tests","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 40 sınavın 19’unda","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۹ آزمون از ۴۰ آزمونِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"Planning a research project","tr":"Bir araştırma projesi planlamak","fa":"برنامه‌ریزی یک پروژه‌ی پژوهشی"},"asks":{"en":"Two students plan a project on repairing and reusing clothes: why they chose the topic, which methods they will use, and what they expect to find for six kinds of clothing.","tr":"İki öğrenci giysileri onarma ve yeniden kullanma üzerine bir proje planlıyor: konuyu neden seçtikleri, hangi yöntemleri kullanacakları ve altı giysi türü için ne bulmayı bekledikleri.","fa":"دو دانشجو برای پروژه‌ای درباره‌ی تعمیر و استفاده‌ی دوباره از لباس برنامه می‌ریزند: چرا این موضوع را انتخاب کردند، از چه روش‌هایی استفاده می‌کنند و برای شش نوع لباس انتظار چه نتیجه‌ای دارند."},"fields":["Why this topic","Methods","Rejected methods","Six kinds of clothing"],"words":[{"a":"what got me thinking","b":"what made me interested","tr":"beni düşündüren şey","fa":"چیزی که مرا به فکر انداخت"},{"a":"a gap in the research","b":"hardly anyone has studied it","tr":"araştırmada bir boşluk","fa":"خلأ پژوهشی"},{"a":"participants","b":"people who take part","tr":"katılımcılar","fa":"شرکت‌کننده‌ها"},{"a":"questionnaire","b":"a list of questions people answer","tr":"anket","fa":"پرسشنامه"},{"a":"interview","b":"talk to someone and ask questions","tr":"görüşme yapmak","fa":"مصاحبه"},{"a":"confidential","b":"secret / not shared","tr":"gizli","fa":"محرمانه"},{"a":"hand down","b":"pass on to a younger person","tr":"küçüklere devretmek","fa":"به کوچک‌ترها دادن"},{"a":"a specialist","b":"someone trained to do it","tr":"uzman","fa":"متخصص"},{"a":"fabric","b":"material / cloth","tr":"kumaş","fa":"پارچه"},{"a":"second-hand","b":"used before / sold on","tr":"ikinci el","fa":"دست‌دوم"},{"a":"fair enough","b":"OK, I accept that","tr":"peki, haklısın","fa":"باشه، قبول"}],"traps":[{"en":"One student suggests a method and the other gives a reason against it (\"a month is too long\"). If the first student agrees (\"fair enough\"), the method is dropped.","tr":"Bir öğrenci bir yöntem önerir, diğeri karşı bir neden verir (\"bir ay çok uzun\"). İlki kabul ederse (\"fair enough\"), yöntem bırakılır.","fa":"یک دانشجو روشی پیشنهاد می‌کند و دیگری دلیلی علیه آن می‌آورد («یک ماه خیلی طولانی است»). اگر اولی قبول کند («fair enough»)، آن روش کنار گذاشته می‌شود."},{"en":"\"Everyone thinks they’re too expensive to repair, but actually...\" The box may contain the popular belief as a distractor. Wait for \"actually\".","tr":"\"Herkes onarmanın çok pahalı olduğunu sanıyor ama aslında...\" Kutuda yaygın inanış çeldirici olarak bulunabilir. \"Actually\"yi bekle.","fa":"«همه فکر می‌کنند تعمیرش خیلی گران است، اما در واقع...». ممکن است باور رایج به‌عنوان گزینه‌ی انحرافی در کادر باشد. منتظر «actually» بمان."}],"example":{"lines":[["Student 1","Shall we film the workshop?"],["Student 2","We’d need everyone’s permission, and that could take weeks."],["Student 1","Fair enough. Let’s just take notes, then."]],"item":"Will they film the workshop?","answer":"No","why":{"en":"Filming is suggested, a problem is given, and \"fair enough\" accepts the problem. They will take notes instead.","tr":"Film çekmek öneriliyor, bir sorun söyleniyor ve \"fair enough\" sorunu kabul ediyor. Onun yerine not alacaklar.","fa":"فیلم‌برداری پیشنهاد می‌شود، مشکلی گفته می‌شود و «fair enough» آن را قبول می‌کند. به جایش یادداشت برمی‌دارند."}}},{"id":"L3-science","ctx":["L3-science"],"title":{"en":"Nature, environment and experiments","tr":"Doğa, çevre ve deneyler","fa":"طبیعت، محیط زیست و آزمایش"},"asks":{"en":"Two students, sometimes with a tutor, plan or review a project on an experiment, an animal or plant, the sea, a volcano or recycling. Questions ask what they decide, what they think of a source or a method, what went wrong and what they will do next.","tr":"İki öğrenci, bazen bir hocayla, bir deney, bir hayvan ya da bitki, deniz, bir yanardağ ya da geri dönüşüm üzerine bir projeyi planlar ya da değerlendirir. Sorular neye karar verdiklerini, bir kaynak ya da yöntem hakkında ne düşündüklerini, neyin ters gittiğini ve sırada ne yapacaklarını sorar.","fa":"دو دانشجو، گاهی با یک استاد، پروژه‌ای درباره‌ی یک آزمایش، یک حیوان یا گیاه، دریا، یک آتشفشان یا بازیافت را برنامه‌ریزی یا بررسی می‌کنند. سؤال‌ها می‌پرسند به چه تصمیمی می‌رسند، درباره‌ی یک منبع یا روش چه فکر می‌کنند، چه چیزی خراب شد و قدم بعدی‌شان چیست."},"fields":["What was the aim of the experiment?","What went wrong with the first method?","What do they decide to change?","Which TWO findings surprised them?","Complete the flow-chart of the procedure."],"words":[{"a":"experiment","b":"the test we ran","tr":"deney","fa":"آزمایش"},{"a":"hypothesis","b":"what we expected to find","tr":"hipotez","fa":"فرضیه"},{"a":"sample","b":"the seeds we tested / the group","tr":"örneklem","fa":"نمونه"},{"a":"variable","b":"the thing we changed","tr":"değişken","fa":"متغیر"},{"a":"results","b":"what we found","tr":"sonuçlar","fa":"نتیجه‌ها"},{"a":"unexpected","b":"we didn't predict that","tr":"beklenmedik","fa":"غیرمنتظره"},{"a":"reliable","b":"we can trust it","tr":"güvenilir","fa":"قابل اعتماد"},{"a":"measure","b":"record how much or how tall","tr":"ölçmek","fa":"اندازه گرفتن"},{"a":"species","b":"kinds of animal or plant","tr":"tür","fa":"گونه"},{"a":"extinct","b":"died out / no longer exists","tr":"soyu tükenmiş","fa":"منقرض"},{"a":"sustainable","b":"doesn't harm the planet","tr":"sürdürülebilir","fa":"پایدار"},{"a":"recycle","b":"use the material again","tr":"geri dönüştürmek","fa":"بازیافت کردن"},{"a":"procedure","b":"the steps we followed","tr":"işlem sırası","fa":"روش کار"}],"traps":[{"en":"Flow-charts: steps are not always said in time order (\"before that, we soaked them\"). Put them in the order they happened.","tr":"Akış şemaları: adımlar her zaman zaman sırasıyla söylenmez (\"ondan önce onları ıslattık\"). Onları olduğu sıraya koy.","fa":"فلوچارت‌ها: مرحله‌ها همیشه به ترتیب زمانی گفته نمی‌شوند («قبلش خیسشان کردیم»). به ترتیبی که اتفاق افتادند بچینشان."},{"en":"Result against expectation: \"we thought light would matter most, but actually temperature did\".","tr":"Beklentiye karşı sonuç: \"ışığın en önemli olduğunu sanıyorduk ama aslında sıcaklıkmış\".","fa":"نتیجه در برابر انتظار: «فکر می‌کردیم نور از همه مهم‌تر است، ولی در واقع دما بود»."}],"example":{"lines":[["Tutor","What affected germination most?"],["Student","We expected light to make the biggest difference."],["Student","But in fact the seeds we kept warm grew fastest, whatever the light."]],"item":"Which factor had the greatest effect?  A light   B temperature   C water","answer":"B","why":{"en":"Light was the expectation. \"In fact\" introduces the result: the warm seeds grew fastest, so temperature.","tr":"Işık beklentiydi. \"In fact\" sonucu getiriyor: sıcak tutulan tohumlar en hızlı büyüdü, yani sıcaklık.","fa":"نور انتظارشان بود. «In fact» نتیجه را می‌آورد: دانه‌های گرم سریع‌تر رشد کردند، پس دما."}},"general":true,"patterns":["L3-science"],"often":{"pattern":"L3-science","n":19,"of":40,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 19 of the last 40 tests","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 40 sınavın 19’unda","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۹ آزمون از ۴۰ آزمونِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"Two pairs, then a box of eight","tr":"İki çift soru, sonra sekizli bir kutu","fa":"دو جفت سؤال، بعد یک کادر هشت‌تایی"},"body":{"en":"Questions 21-22 and 23-24 each ask you to choose TWO letters, A-E. After a short break, Questions 25-30 list six items: choose SIX answers from a box of eight, A-H, each letter once.","tr":"Soru 21-22 ve 23-24’ün her biri A-E arasından İKİ harf seçmeni ister. Kısa bir aradan sonra Soru 25-30 altı öğe sıralar: A-H arasındaki sekiz seçenekten ALTI cevap seç, her harf bir kez.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۲۱-۲۲ و ۲۳-۲۴ هر کدام می‌خواهند از A تا E دو حرف انتخاب کنی. بعد از یک مکث کوتاه، سؤال‌های ۲۵ تا ۳۰ شش مورد را فهرست می‌کنند: از کادر هشت‌تایی A تا H شش جواب انتخاب کن، هر حرف یک بار."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"Agreed, or dropped?","tr":"Kabul mü, ret mi?","fa":"پذیرفته یا کنار گذاشته؟"},"steps":[{"en":"For each option you hear, decide: did both students accept it, or did one of them give a reason against it?","tr":"Duyduğun her seçenek için karar ver: iki öğrenci de kabul etti mi, yoksa biri karşı bir neden mi verdi?","fa":"برای هر گزینه‌ای که می‌شنوی تصمیم بگیر: هر دو دانشجو قبولش کردند یا یکی دلیلی علیه آن آورد؟"},{"en":"In the box task, the six items come in order. Read the box twice in the break so you know the eight ideas well.","tr":"Kutu görevinde altı öğe sırayla gelir. Arada kutuyu iki kez oku ki sekiz fikri iyi bil.","fa":"در تمرین کادر، شش مورد به ترتیب می‌آیند. در مکث کادر را دو بار بخوان تا هشت ایده را خوب بشناسی."},{"en":"Cross out each letter you use: a letter is not used twice.","tr":"Kullandığın her harfin üstünü çiz: bir harf iki kez kullanılmaz.","fa":"هر حرفی را که استفاده می‌کنی خط بزن: یک حرف دو بار به کار نمی‌رود."}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"The belief, then the fact","tr":"Önce inanış, sonra gerçek","fa":"اول باور، بعد واقعیت"},"body":{"en":"Students often mention what \"everyone thinks\" or what \"some people do\" before saying what they really believe. The box usually contains both. The answer follows \"actually\", \"in my experience\" or \"the thing is\".","tr":"Öğrenciler gerçekte neye inandıklarını söylemeden önce çoğu zaman \"herkesin ne düşündüğünden\" ya da \"bazı insanların ne yaptığından\" söz eder. Kutuda genelde ikisi de bulunur. Cevap \"actually\", \"in my experience\" ya da \"the thing is\"ten sonra gelir.","fa":"دانشجوها اغلب قبل از گفتن نظر واقعی‌شان از چیزی که «همه فکر می‌کنند» یا کاری که «بعضی‌ها می‌کنند» حرف می‌زنند. کادر معمولاً هر دو را دارد. جواب بعد از «actually»، «in my experience» یا «the thing is» می‌آید."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"One box item, step by step","tr":"Bir kutu öğesi, adım adım","fa":"یک مورد کادر، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"What do the students say about each item? Box: A often lost  B usually repaired at home  C too expensive to replace","item":"umbrellas","lines":[["Student 1","People think umbrellas are too expensive to replace."],["Student 2","Not really, they’re cheap. The thing is, everyone leaves them on buses and trains."]],"answer":"A","walk":[{"en":"C is the belief that \"people think\", and Student 2 rejects it.","tr":"C, \"insanların düşündüğü\" inanış ve 2. öğrenci onu reddediyor.","fa":"C باوری است که «مردم فکر می‌کنند» و دانشجوی دوم ردش می‌کند."},{"en":"\"The thing is\" introduces the real point.","tr":"\"The thing is\" asıl noktayı getiriyor.","fa":"«the thing is» نکته‌ی اصلی را می‌آورد."},{"en":"Leaving umbrellas on buses = they are often lost: A.","tr":"Şemsiyeleri otobüste bırakmak = sık sık kaybolurlar: A.","fa":"جا گذاشتن چتر در اتوبوس یعنی اغلب گم می‌شوند: A."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"Student A: \"Let’s interview the shop managers.\" Student B: \"They’re far too busy at this time of year.\" Student A: \"You’re right. Let’s use the online survey only.\" Will they interview the managers?","options":["No","Yes","Only some of them"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"A reason against the idea, then \"You’re right\": the interviews are dropped.","tr":"Fikre karşı bir neden, sonra \"You’re right\": görüşmeler bırakılıyor.","fa":"دلیلی علیه ایده و بعد «You’re right»: مصاحبه‌ها کنار گذاشته می‌شوند."}},"remember":{"en":"Choose only what both speakers accept, and wait for \"actually\" after a popular belief.","tr":"Yalnızca iki konuşanın da kabul ettiğini seç; yaygın bir inanıştan sonra \"actually\"yi bekle.","fa":"فقط چیزی را انتخاب کن که هر دو گوینده قبول دارند و بعد از یک باور رایج منتظر «actually» بمان."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x03-l3-e","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-03","unit":"x03-l3"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"listening","part":"Listening Part 3","title":{"en":"A project on clothes repair","tr":"Giysi onarımı üzerine bir proje","fa":"پروژه‌ای درباره‌ی تعمیر لباس"},"timed":7,"ctx":["L3-science"],"script":[{"who":"Tamsin","line":"So, Kofi, we need to send Dr Ellery our research topic by Friday. Are we still agreed on clothes repair?"},{"who":"Kofi","line":"I think so. For me it really started with that lecture on textile waste. I hadn't realised how many clothes end up in landfill after being worn only a few times. That was what got me thinking."},{"who":"Tamsin","line":"Same for me. And when I looked for articles, I found loads of studies on recycling clothes, but hardly anyone has studied repair: who repairs clothes, and why. So there's a real gap."},{"who":"Kofi","line":"That's a good point to put in the proposal. I also thought it'd be easy to find people to take part. Everyone wears clothes, after all."},{"who":"Tamsin","line":"I'm not so sure. People might not want to admit they throw things away. Anyway, Dr Ellery actually suggested we look at clothes swapping, didn't she?"},{"who":"Kofi","line":"She did, but she said it was up to us. And I know you make some of your own clothes, Tamsin, but I can't sew at all, so it's not as if we're both experts."},{"who":"Tamsin","line":"True. OK, methods. I think an online questionnaire is essential: it's the only way to get enough responses in the time we have."},{"who":"Kofi","line":"Agreed. And I'd like to talk to people who repair clothes for a living. There are three tailors near the station, and the woman at the dry cleaner's does alterations."},{"who":"Tamsin","line":"Interviews with them would be great. What about asking people to keep a diary of every repair they do for a month?"},{"who":"Kofi","line":"It's a nice idea, but a month is too long. People would give up after a week."},{"who":"Tamsin","line":"Fair enough. I'd love to watch what goes on at the repair café in the library, too."},{"who":"Kofi","line":"Me too, but it only runs on the first Sunday of the month, and the next one is after our deadline. And we can't get sales figures from the shops; I asked, and they said it's confidential."},{"who":"Tamsin","line":"So, the questionnaire and the interviews, then. How many people should we aim for with the questionnaire?"},{"who":"Kofi","line":"Dr Ellery said at least a hundred, or the results won't mean very much. I'll ask the students' union to share the link."},{"who":"Tamsin","line":"Good. Now, we said we'd look at different kinds of clothing. Shall we go through the list and decide what we expect to find for each one?"},{"who":"Kofi","line":"Good idea. Jeans first. People don't throw jeans away when fashions change, do they? They wear them until they fall apart."},{"who":"Tamsin","line":"And when they tear, most people just repair them at home. A patch on the knee, maybe some stitching. You don't take jeans to a tailor."},{"who":"Kofi","line":"No. What about school uniforms? Some families must buy new ones every year."},{"who":"Tamsin","line":"Some do, but in my experience they're mostly handed down to younger brothers and sisters. My little sister wore my old school jumper for three years."},{"who":"Kofi","line":"Right. Leather jackets are interesting. Everyone thinks they're too expensive to repair, but actually a new zip or a new lining doesn't cost much. The thing is, you can't do it yourself. You need a specialist."},{"who":"Tamsin","line":"So it's professionals who repair those. Then sportswear. That's the opposite case, I think."},{"who":"Kofi","line":"Yes. It's cheap, but the stretchy synthetic fabric is really hard to sew neatly, even on a machine. The seams just pull apart again."},{"who":"Tamsin","line":"Exactly, the material's the problem. Winter coats?"},{"who":"Kofi","line":"They last for years, so people don't often repair them, but when they're tired of them, they don't throw them away either. They sell them online. There's a huge second-hand market for good coats."},{"who":"Tamsin","line":"That's true. I bought mine second-hand. And finally, party clothes."},{"who":"Kofi","line":"People wear a party dress or a suit maybe two or three times. It's not that the fashion changes; they just don't want to be seen in the same thing again. So they hardly ever get worn out before they're replaced."},{"who":"Tamsin","line":"Yes, that's the saddest category. OK, let's write all this up as our predictions, and then see if the questionnaire agrees with us."},{"who":"Kofi","line":"Great. I'll draft the questions tonight and send them to you."}],"groups":[{"instruction":"Questions 21-22. Choose TWO letters, A-E.","qtype":"mcq2","questions":[{"n":21,"n2":22,"kind":"mcq2","prompt":"Which TWO reasons do the students give for choosing clothes repair as their topic?","options":["A It will be easy to find people to take part.","B Their tutor suggested it.","C A lecture made them interested in it.","D Very little research has been done on it.","E They both make their own clothes."],"correct":[2,3],"evidence":"That was what got me thinking","trap":["TR-ruledout","TR-paraphrase"],"why":{"en":"C the lecture on textile waste \"got me thinking\", and D \"hardly anyone has studied repair\". Tamsin doubts it will be easy to find participants, the tutor suggested a different topic, and Kofi cannot sew.","tr":"C tekstil atığı dersi \"beni düşündürdü\" ve D \"neredeyse kimse onarımı araştırmamış\". Tamsin katılımcı bulmanın kolay olacağından şüpheli, hoca başka bir konu önermişti ve Kofi dikiş dikemiyor.","fa":"C درس پسماند پارچه «مرا به فکر انداخت» و D «تقریباً هیچ‌کس تعمیر را بررسی نکرده». تامسین شک دارد پیدا کردن شرکت‌کننده آسان باشد، استاد موضوع دیگری پیشنهاد کرده بود و کوفی خیاطی بلد نیست."}}]},{"instruction":"Questions 23-24. Choose TWO letters, A-E.","qtype":"mcq2","questions":[{"n":23,"n2":24,"kind":"mcq2","prompt":"Which TWO methods will the students use?","options":["A a diary kept by participants for a month","B an online questionnaire","C watching people at a repair café","D interviews with people who repair clothes for a living","E sales figures from local shops"],"correct":[1,3],"evidence":"I think an online questionnaire is essential","trap":["TR-ruledout"],"why":{"en":"B the questionnaire is \"essential\" and D they agree on interviews with tailors. The diary is too long, the repair café is after the deadline, and sales figures are confidential.","tr":"B anket \"şart\" ve D terzilerle görüşmede anlaşıyorlar. Günlük çok uzun sürer, onarım kafesi son tarihten sonra ve satış rakamları gizli.","fa":"B پرسشنامه «ضروری» است و D روی مصاحبه با خیاط‌ها توافق می‌کنند. دفترچه‌ی روزانه خیلی طول می‌کشد، کافه‌ی تعمیر بعد از مهلت است و آمار فروش محرمانه است."}}]},{"instruction":"Questions 25-30. What do the students expect to find about each of the following kinds of clothing? Choose SIX answers from the box and write the correct letter, A-H, next to Questions 25-30.","qtype":"matching","bank":["A rarely worn out before they are replaced","B difficult to repair because of the material","C often passed on to younger family members","D usually thrown away when fashions change","E often repaired at home","F too expensive to repair","G repaired mainly by professionals","H usually sold second-hand"],"questions":[{"n":25,"kind":"match","prompt":"jeans","correct":4,"evidence":"most people just repair them at home","why":{"en":"Not thrown away when fashions change (D is ruled out): \"most people just repair them at home\".","tr":"Moda değişince atılmıyor (D eleniyor): \"çoğu insan onları evde onarıyor\".","fa":"وقتی مد عوض می‌شود دور انداخته نمی‌شوند (D رد می‌شود): «بیشتر مردم در خانه تعمیرشان می‌کنند»."},"trap":["TR-ruledout","PARA-opinion"]},{"n":26,"kind":"match","prompt":"school uniforms","correct":2,"evidence":"they're mostly handed down to younger brothers and sisters","why":{"en":"\"Mostly handed down to younger brothers and sisters\" = passed on to younger family members.","tr":"\"Çoğunlukla küçük kardeşlere devrediliyor\" = ailedeki küçüklere geçiyor.","fa":"«بیشتر به خواهر و برادرهای کوچک‌تر داده می‌شوند» یعنی به اعضای کوچک‌تر خانواده می‌رسند."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":27,"kind":"match","prompt":"leather jackets","correct":6,"evidence":"You need a specialist","why":{"en":"\"Everyone thinks they’re too expensive to repair\" (F), \"but actually\" the repair is cheap; \"you need a specialist\".","tr":"\"Herkes onarmanın çok pahalı olduğunu sanıyor\" (F), \"ama aslında\" onarım ucuz; \"bir uzmana ihtiyacın var\".","fa":"«همه فکر می‌کنند تعمیرشان خیلی گران است» (F)، «اما در واقع» تعمیر ارزان است؛ «به یک متخصص نیاز داری»."},"trap":["TR-ruledout","PARA-opinion"]},{"n":28,"kind":"match","prompt":"sportswear","correct":1,"evidence":"the material's the problem","why":{"en":"The stretchy synthetic fabric is hard to sew: \"the material’s the problem\".","tr":"Esnek sentetik kumaşı dikmek zor: \"sorun malzemede\".","fa":"پارچه‌ی کش‌دار مصنوعی را سخت می‌شود دوخت: «مشکل جنسِ پارچه است»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":29,"kind":"match","prompt":"winter coats","correct":7,"evidence":"They sell them online","why":{"en":"People do not throw coats away: \"They sell them online... a huge second-hand market.\"","tr":"İnsanlar montları atmıyor: \"İnternetten satıyorlar... büyük bir ikinci el pazarı var.\"","fa":"مردم پالتو را دور نمی‌اندازند: «آنلاین می‌فروشندشان... بازار دست‌دوم بزرگی هست»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":30,"kind":"match","prompt":"party clothes","correct":0,"evidence":"they hardly ever get worn out before they're replaced","why":{"en":"\"It’s not that the fashion changes\" (D is ruled out); \"they hardly ever get worn out before they’re replaced\".","tr":"\"Mesele modanın değişmesi değil\" (D eleniyor); \"değiştirilmeden önce neredeyse hiç eskimiyorlar\".","fa":"«مسئله عوض شدن مد نیست» (D رد می‌شود)؛ «تقریباً هیچ‌وقت قبل از اینکه کنار گذاشته شوند کهنه نمی‌شوند»."},"trap":["TR-ruledout"]}]}],"audio":{"voices":{"Announcer":{"accent":"British (standard Southern)","gender":"M","tts":{"engine":"kokoro","voice":"bm_george"},"role":"Recorded rubric"},"Tamsin":{"accent":"British (Southern English)","gender":"F","tts":{"engine":"kokoro","voice":"bf_emma"},"role":"Student"},"Kofi":{"accent":"Northern English","gender":"M","tts":{"engine":"piper","voice":"en_GB-northern_english_male-medium"},"role":"Student"}},"sequence":[{"type":"announcer","text":"Part 3. You will hear two students, Tamsin and Kofi, planning a research project on repairing and reusing clothes. First, you have some time to look at Questions 21 to 24."},{"type":"pause","seconds":30,"note":"reading time, Questions 21-24"},{"type":"announcer","text":"Now listen carefully and answer Questions 21 to 24."},{"type":"sfx","note":"university library study room: very low background murmur"},{"type":"lines","from":0,"to":13},{"type":"announcer","text":"Before you hear the rest of the discussion, you have some time to look at Questions 25 to 30."},{"type":"pause","seconds":30,"note":"reading time, Questions 25-30"},{"type":"announcer","text":"Now listen and answer Questions 25 to 30."},{"type":"lines","from":14,"to":27},{"type":"announcer","text":"That is the end of Part 3. You now have half a minute to check your answers.","after":30}]},"id":"c-x03-l3-d","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-03","unit":"x03-l3"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"Information that is \"confidential\" is...","options":["free to download","out of date","kept private"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"Confidential = not shared with other people.","tr":"Confidential = başkalarıyla paylaşılmayan.","fa":"confidential یعنی با دیگران به اشتراک گذاشته نمی‌شود."}},{"tests":"paraphrase","point":1,"prompt":"Which phrase means \"passed on to a younger person\"?","options":["handed in","handed down","handed out"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"Clothes handed down go to a younger brother, sister or relative. Handed in = given to a teacher or office.","tr":"Handed down giysiler küçük bir kardeşe ya da akrabaya geçer. Handed in = bir öğretmene ya da büroya teslim edilen.","fa":"لباسی که handed down می‌شود به خواهر، برادر یا فامیل کوچک‌تر می‌رسد. handed in یعنی تحویل به معلم یا دفتر."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"A box has eight options and there are six items. How many letters will you use?","options":["six, each once","all eight","six, one of them twice"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"\"Choose SIX answers from the box\": six different letters, two left over.","tr":"\"Kutudan ALTI cevap seç\": altı farklı harf, ikisi artar.","fa":"«شش جواب از کادر انتخاب کن»: شش حرف متفاوت، دو تا اضافه می‌مانند."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"\"People assume old bikes get thrown away, but in fact most are sold on.\" What does the speaker say about old bikes?","options":["They are usually thrown away.","They are rarely used.","They are usually sold second-hand."],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"\"People assume\" gives the distractor; \"in fact most are sold on\" gives the answer.","tr":"\"People assume\" çeldiriciyi verir; \"aslında çoğu satılıyor\" cevabı verir.","fa":"«people assume» گزینه‌ی انحرافی را می‌دهد؛ «در واقع بیشترشان فروخته می‌شوند» جواب را."}},{"tests":"trap","point":2,"prompt":"\"How about a focus group?\" \"It would be hard to get everyone together.\" \"True. Let’s leave it.\" Will they use a focus group?","options":["Yes","No","Later in the project"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"A problem, then agreement (\"True. Let’s leave it.\"): the idea is dropped.","tr":"Bir sorun, sonra onay (\"Doğru. Bırakalım.\"): fikir bırakılıyor.","fa":"یک مشکل و بعد موافقت («درست است. ولش کنیم»): ایده کنار گذاشته می‌شود."}}],"id":"c-x03-l3-x","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-03","unit":"x03-l3"}}; })(globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS = globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS || {});
